/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Detail Structure Padding, Data Alignment, and sizeof\(struct\) calculations, explaining #pragma pack\(1\) and __attribute__\(\(packed\)\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Structure Padding and Data Alignment in C:) Tj
T*
(   1. Microprocessor Hardware Alignment Constraints:) Tj
T*
(   - Modern 32-bit and 64-bit microprocessors access memory in aligned word chunks \(4-byte or) Tj
T*
(   8-byte boundaries\).) Tj
T*
(   - Reading an unaligned 4-byte integer spanning two cache lines requires two memory bus cycles) Tj
T*
(   and bitwise shifting, significantly degrading performance.) Tj
T*
(   - Alignment Rules:) Tj
T*
(   - 1-byte char can reside at any address.) Tj
T*
(   - 2-byte short must align to an even address \(multiple of 2\).) Tj
T*
(   - 4-byte int/float must align to addresses divisible by 4.) Tj
T*
(   - 8-byte double/pointer must align to addresses divisible by 8.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Structure Padding Walkthrough:) Tj
T*
(   Consider:) Tj
T*
(   struct Sample {) Tj
T*
(   char a; /* 1 byte at offset 0 */) Tj
T*
(   /* 3 padding bytes inserted here to align 'b' to multiple of 4! */) Tj
T*
(   int b; /* 4 bytes at offset 4 */) Tj
T*
(   char c; /* 1 byte at offset 8 */) Tj
T*
(   /* 3 tail padding bytes added to make entire struct multiple of 4! */) Tj
T*
(   };) Tj
T*
(   Total sizeof\(struct Sample\) = 1 + 3 + 4 + 1 + 3 = 12 bytes! \(Not 6 bytes!\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Disabling Padding: Packed Structures:) Tj
T*
(   - In networking protocols and binary file formats, padding wastes bandwidth and destroys field) Tj
T*
(   offsets.) Tj
T*
(   - GCC / Clang: struct __attribute__\(\(packed\)\) PackedSample { ... };) Tj
T*
(   - MSVC / Standard: #pragma pack\(push, 1\) ... #pragma pack\(pop\)) Tj
T*
(   - Tradeoff: Packed structures eliminate padding but incur memory read speed penalties on) Tj
T*
(   architectures that forbid unaligned access \(e.g. ARM\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Demonstrative ANSI C Program:) Tj
T*
ET

