(   [Problem Statement]: Explain Tagged / Discriminated Unions in C, implementing a type-safe polymorphic biological entity container.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Tagged \(Discriminated\) Unions in C:) Tj
T*
(   1. Conceptual Purpose:) Tj
T*
(   Because C unions share memory, a raw union has no built-in mechanism to record WHICH member is) Tj
T*
(   currently active. Accessing an inactive member reads garbage or corrupted data.) Tj
T*
(   A Tagged Union wraps an enum tag and the union together inside a struct, providing type-safe) Tj
T*
(   pseudo-polymorphism.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Architecture:) Tj
T*
(   struct TaggedContainer {) Tj
T*
(   enum TypeDiscriminator type;) Tj
T*
(   union Payload data;) Tj
T*
(   };) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Complete ANSI C Source Code \(Biological Reagent Assay\):) Tj
T*
(   #include <stdio.h>) Tj
T*
(   #include <string.h>) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   typedef enum {) Tj
T*
(   TYPE_DNA,) Tj
T*
