(   [Problem Statement]: Detail Bit-Fields in C, explaining packing syntax, member constraints, hardware register mapping, and endianness issues.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Bit-Fields in C: Syntax, Constraints, and Systems Applications:) Tj
T*
(   1. Syntax and Definition:) Tj
T*
(   Bit-fields permit declaring structure members with explicit, custom bit widths, packing) Tj
T*
(   multiple variables into single bytes/words:) Tj
T*
(   struct BitFieldDefinition {) Tj
T*
(   type member_name : bit_width;) Tj
T*
(   };) Tj
T*
(   - Allowed Types: unsigned int, signed int, _Bool \(C99\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Memory Conservation Example:) Tj
T*
(   struct PacketHeader {) Tj
T*
(   unsigned int version : 4; /* 4 bits \(0-15\) */) Tj
T*
(   unsigned int header_len : 4; /* 4 bits \(0-15\) */) Tj
T*
(   unsigned int tos : 8; /* 8 bits \(0-255\) */) Tj
T*
(   unsigned int total_len : 16; /* 16 bits \(0-65535\) */) Tj
T*
(   };) Tj
T*
(   Packs all 4 fields into exactly 32 bits \(4 bytes\)!) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Strict Bit-Field Constraints:) Tj
T*
(   - No Address-Of Operator \(&\): Bit-fields do NOT have distinct byte memory addresses. Code like) Tj
T*
(   &hdr.version causes an immediate compile error!) Tj
T*
(   - No Array of Bit-Fields: Arrays require contiguous element byte addresses.) Tj
T*
(   - No sizeof on Bit-Field Members: sizeof\(hdr.version\) is illegal.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Endianness and Portability Caveat:) Tj
T*
(   The ISO C standard leaves the layout order of bits within an integer word \(low-order to) Tj
T*
(   high-order vs high-order to low-order\) IMPLEMENTATION-DEFINED!) Tj
T*
(   Bit-fields written on x86 \(little-endian\) are reversed relative to network protocols or) Tj
T*
(   big-endian processors.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   5. Complete ANSI C Demonstration Program:) Tj
T*
(   #include <stdio.h>) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   struct BioreactorStatus {) Tj
T*
(   unsigned int impeller_active : 1; /* 1 bit: 0 or 1 */) Tj
T*
(   unsigned int heater_active : 1; /* 1 bit: 0 or 1 */) Tj
T*
(   unsigned int acid_valve_open : 1; /* 1 bit: 0 or 1 */) Tj
T*
(   unsigned int base_valve_open : 1; /* 1 bit: 0 or 1 */) Tj
T*
(   unsigned int sensor_fault : 1; /* 1 bit: 0 or 1 */) Tj
T*
(   unsigned int alarm_severity : 3; /* 3 bits: 0 to 7 */) Tj
T*
(   };) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   int main\(void\) {) Tj
T*
(   struct BioreactorStatus status = {0};) Tj
T*
(   status.impeller_active = 1;) Tj
T*
(   status.acid_valve_open = 1;) Tj
T*
(   status.alarm_severity = 5;) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   printf\("Bioreactor packed status footprint: %zu byte\(s\)\\n", sizeof\(status\)\);) Tj
T*
(   printf\("Impeller: %u | Acid Valve: %u | Alarm Severity: %u of 7\\n",) Tj
T*
(   status.impeller_active, status.acid_valve_open, status.alarm_severity\);) Tj
T*
() Tj
