(   [Problem Statement]: Explain typedef and enum in C, detailing type aliasing, code readability, function pointer shortcuts, and underlying integral types.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   typedef and enum in C:) Tj
T*
(   1. The typedef Facility:) Tj
T*
(   - Purpose: Establishes a synonym \(alias\) for an existing data type. Does NOT create a new type.) Tj
T*
(   - Syntax: typedef existing_type new_alias_name;) Tj
T*
(   - Enhancing Code Portability:) Tj
T*
(   typedef unsigned long long uint64_t;) Tj
T*
(   - Simplifying Structure Definitions:) Tj
T*
(   typedef struct Node { int data; struct Node *next; } Node;) Tj
T*
(   Allows declaring Node n1; without prefixing 'struct'.) Tj
T*
(   - Simplifying Function Pointers:) Tj
T*
(   typedef double \(*MathFunc\)\(double, double\);) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. The enum Facility:) Tj
T*
(   - Purpose: Defines a user-defined enumeration type consisting of named integer constants.) Tj
T*
(   - Syntax: enum Colors { RED, GREEN, BLUE };) Tj
T*
(   - Auto-Numbering: RED = 0, GREEN = 1, BLUE = 2.) Tj
T*
(   - Custom Numbering:) Tj
T*
(   enum Response { SUCCESS = 200, NOT_FOUND = 404, SERVER_ERROR = 500 };) Tj
T*
(   - Underlying Type: Enumerations are internally represented as signed integer \(int\) values.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
