(   [Problem Statement]: Explain Random Access File Handling in C, detailing fseek\(\), ftell\(\), rewind\(\), and SEEK_SET, SEEK_CUR, SEEK_END origin flags.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Random Access File Handling in C:) Tj
T*
(   1. Concept of File Positioning:) Tj
T*
(   Unlike sequential file access, random access moves the file stream position indicator directly) Tj
T*
(   to any arbitrary byte offset without reading intervening data.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. The fseek\(\) Function:) Tj
T*
(   int fseek\(FILE *stream, long offset, int origin\);) Tj
T*
(   Origins:) Tj
T*
(   - SEEK_SET: Offset is relative to the start of the file \(offset >= 0\).) Tj
T*
(   - SEEK_CUR: Offset is relative to current file position \(offset can be positive or negative\).) Tj
T*
(   - SEEK_END: Offset is relative to end of file \(offset typically <= 0\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. The ftell\(\) Function:) Tj
T*
(   long ftell\(FILE *stream\);) Tj
T*
(   Returns current byte position offset from beginning of file, or -1L on error.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Computing File Size via fseek and ftell:) Tj
T*
(   fseek\(fp, 0L, SEEK_END\);) Tj
T*
(   long file_size = ftell\(fp\);) Tj
T*
(   fseek\(fp, 0L, SEEK_SET\); /* Or rewind\(fp\); */) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   5. Complete ANSI C Demonstration Program:) Tj
T*
(   #include <stdio.h>) Tj
T*
(   #include <stdlib.h>) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   int main\(void\) {) Tj
T*
(   FILE *fp = fopen\("records.bin", "wb+"\);) Tj
T*
(   if \(!fp\) return 1;) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   /* Write 10 integers \(0, 10, 20, ..., 90\) */) Tj
T*
(   for \(int i = 0; i < 10; i++\) {) Tj
T*
(   int val = i * 10;) Tj
T*
(   fwrite\(&val, sizeof\(int\), 1, fp\);) Tj
T*
(   }) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   /* Random access: Seek directly to the 5th integer \(index 4\) */) Tj
T*
(   fseek\(fp, 4 * sizeof\(int\), SEEK_SET\);) Tj
T*
(   int read_val;) Tj
T*
(   fread\(&read_val, sizeof\(int\), 1, fp\);) Tj
T*
(   printf\("Randomly retrieved 5th record: %d \(Expected: 40\)\\n", read_val\);) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
