(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze the dangerous while \(!feof\(fp\)\) anti-pattern in C file handling, explaining why feof\(\) only triggers AFTER read failure.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   The Fatal while \(!feof\(fp\)\) Anti-Pattern in C:) Tj
T*
(   1. The Common Flawed Code Pattern:) Tj
T*
(   while \(!feof\(fp\)\) {) Tj
T*
(   fscanf\(fp, "%s", buffer\);) Tj
T*
(   printf\("%s\\n", buffer\);) Tj
T*
(   }) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Why it Fails \(The One-Extra-Iteration Bug\):) Tj
T*
(   - Flaw: The feof\(\) function DOES NOT predict the future!) Tj
T*
(   - In standard ANSI C, the EOF indicator flag is set ONLY AFTER AN I/O OPERATION ATTEMPTS TO) Tj
T*
(   READ BEYOND THE END OF THE FILE AND FAILS!) Tj
T*
(   - Sequence of Events on Final Line:) Tj
T*
(   a. Final data line is read successfully. feof\(fp\) is still FALSE \(0\).) Tj
T*
(   b. Loop repeats because !feof\(fp\) is true.) Tj
T*
(   c. fscanf\(\) attempts to read past EOF, fails, and returns EOF \(-1\).) Tj
T*
(   d. THE BUFFER IS NOT UPDATED!) Tj
T*
(   e. printf\("%s\\n", buffer\) executes AGAIN, printing the final record TWICE!) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. The Correct Idiomatic C Pattern:) Tj
T*
(   Always check the return value of the read function directly in the loop condition:) Tj
T*
(   /* Correct Pattern 1: Formatted input */) Tj
T*
(   while \(fscanf\(fp, "%s", buffer\) == 1\) {) Tj
T*
(   printf\("%s\\n", buffer\);) Tj
T*
(   }) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   /* Correct Pattern 2: Line reading */) Tj
T*
(   while \(fgets\(buffer, sizeof\(buffer\), fp\) != NULL\) {) Tj
T*
(   printf\("%s", buffer\);) Tj
T*
(   }) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   /* Correct Pattern 3: Character reading */) Tj
T*
(   int ch;) Tj
T*
(   while \(\(ch = fgetc\(fp\)\) != EOF\) {) Tj
T*
(   putchar\(ch\);) Tj
T*
(   }) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
