(   incomplete array type:) Tj
T*
(   struct Packet {) Tj
T*
(   int length;) Tj
T*
(   char payload[]; /* Flexible array member: no dimension */) Tj
T*
(   };) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Memory Allocation Pattern:) Tj
T*
(   Allocate the structure size plus the desired dynamic array capacity in a single continuous) Tj
T*
(   malloc\(\) call:) Tj
T*
(   size_t n = 500;) Tj
T*
(   struct Packet *pkt = malloc\(sizeof\(struct Packet\) + \(n * sizeof\(char\)\)\);) Tj
T*
(   pkt->length = n;) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Semantics and Advantages:) Tj
T*
(   - Single Allocation: Structure header and payload reside in a single contiguous heap block,) Tj
T*
(   improving cache locality.) Tj
T*
(   - Single Free: Entire entity is released with a single free\(pkt\).) Tj
T*
(   - sizeof\(struct Packet\) evaluates ONLY to the header members \(payload size is omitted\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Contrast with Legacy 'Struct Hack':) Tj
T*
(   Before C99, programmers used char payload[1]; or char payload[0];, which triggered compiler) Tj
T*
(   bounds warnings or relied on non-standard GCC extensions.) Tj
T*
() Tj
