(   1. The Global errno Variable \(<errno.h>\):) Tj
T*
(   When a standard C library function or system call fails \(e.g. fopen, malloc\), it sets an) Tj
T*
(   integer code in the thread-local global variable 'errno'.) Tj
T*
(   Common error codes:) Tj
T*
(   - ENOENT: No such file or directory.) Tj
T*
(   - EACCES: Permission denied.) Tj
T*
(   - ENOMEM: Cannot allocate memory.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. The perror\(\) Function \(<stdio.h>\):) Tj
T*
(   void perror\(const char *custom_prefix\);) Tj
T*
(   Prints custom_prefix followed by a colon and the human-readable explanation of current errno to) Tj
T*
(   stderr:) Tj
T*
(   perror\("Failed to open sequencing database"\);) Tj
T*
(   Output: "Failed to open sequencing database: No such file or directory".) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. The strerror\(\) Function \(<string.h>\):) Tj
T*
(   char *strerror\(int errnum\);) Tj
T*
(   Returns a pointer to the textual error string corresponding to errnum, allowing formatted) Tj
T*
(   custom logging.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
