(   [Problem Statement]: Explain anonymous unions and anonymous structures in modern C, detailing member flattening.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Anonymous Structures and Unions in C11:) Tj
T*
(   1. Definition:) Tj
T*
(   Introduced in C11, anonymous structures and unions have no tag name and no member variable name) Tj
T*
(   inside an enclosing structure.) Tj
T*
(   Members are directly 'flattened' into the scope of the parent structure!) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Code Example:) Tj
T*
(   #include <stdio.h>) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   struct Vector3D {) Tj
T*
(   struct {) Tj
T*
(   double x, y, z; /* Anonymous structure */) Tj
T*
(   };) Tj
T*
(   int id;) Tj
T*
(   };) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   int main\(void\) {) Tj
T*
(   struct Vector3D v;) Tj
T*
(   /* Accessed directly without intermediate struct tag! */) Tj
T*
